          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Iron deficiency anemia sits in the blood chapter. Which chapter would an underlying bleeding ulcer be coded from?",
          "answer": "A bleeding ulcer would be coded from the chapter that applies to the specific bleeding site. For instance, if the ulcer is in the digestive system, it would be coded from Chapter 11: Diseases of the Digestive System (K00-K95), as noted in the \"ICD-10-CM Chapter 11: diseases of the digestive system (K00-K95)\" document. The same document explains that certain bleeding presentations, such as hematemesis and melena, are categorized within this chapter.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
